      "target": "../sections/sec-front-matter.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "Annif at SemEval-2025 Task 5: Traditional XMTC augmented by LLMs\nOsma Suominen and Juho Inkinen and Mona Lehtinen\nNational Library of Finland, University of Helsinki\nfirstname.lastname@helsinki.fi\nAbstract\nThis paper presents the Annif system in\nSemEval-2025 Task 5 (LLMs4Subjects), which\nfocussed on subject indexing using large lan-\nguage models (LLMs).\nThe task required\ncreating subject predictions for bibliographic\nrecords from the bilingual TIBKAT database\nusing the GND subject vocabulary. Our ap-\nproach combines traditional natural language\nprocessing and machine learning techniques im-\npl",
      "truncated": true,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "draft",
        "text": "Title, authors and abstract of \"Annif at SemEval-2025 Task 5: Traditional XMTC augmented by LLMs\" by Osma Suominen, Juho Inkinen and Mona Lehtinen (National Library of Finland, University of Helsinki). The paper describes the Annif system in the LLMs4Subjects shared task, which asked for GND subject predictions for records of the bilingual TIBKAT database. It combines traditional NLP and machine-learning methods from the Annif toolkit with LLM-based translation and synthetic data generation, and merges predictions from monolingual models. It ranked first in all-subjects and second in tib-core-subjects quantitatively, and fourth qualitatively.",
