        "status": "draft",
        "text": "Analysis (with Table 1, the full development and test results). The English variants beat the German ones in all but one case, which the authors attribute possibly to better English translations or to German's compound-rich structure being harder for traditional pipelines. Synthetic records raised Bonsai's nDCG by about 0.03 (the experimental section gives about 0.02 for the first synthetic part). BMX beat BM, so adding XTransformer helped, while the neural ensembles underperformed on the test set because training and evaluation data were structurally similar. Merging the monolingual predictions beat either language alone; without it they would have ranked 2nd and 3rd. The authors suggest their qualitative 4th place reflects predictions that track existing TIBKAT metadata, where LLM-heavier systems were less constrained, and note that no system exceeded 0.35 F1@5, possibly showing inconsistent TIBKAT subject metadata; they propose nDCG@50 for ranking 50-subject outputs.",
